cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use akrasia in your research, please cite this repository."
title: "akrasia"
abstract: >-
  A diagnostic instrument that measures whether an LLM agent acts on its own
  stated beliefs in a minimal repeated-pricing game, using a two-oracle
  decomposition that separates estimation error (is the stated belief correct?)
  from execution error (does the chosen action follow from that belief?), plus a
  no-training scaffold whose effect is measured through that instrument.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/vmfan/akrasia"
url: "https://github.com/vmfan/akrasia"
authors:
  - family-names: Fan
    given-names: Vincent Marciano
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - sequential decision making
  - knowing-doing gap
  - belief elicitation
  - expected-value oracle
  - agent evaluation
